The cleaned runtime does not call FloPy or MODFLOW. It explicitly constructs the
same confined-aquifer harmonic finite-volume equations and solves them using
general numerical primitives. Original numerical forward serialization, source
and independent backend differences are documented in validation. The small
co-kriging linear system uses its independently validated Schur/Woodbury form
rather than the original general matrix-free Krylov numerical backend.

The original reported variance helper has an independently demonstrated missing
lower-block saddle contribution. It is preserved only as a named source variance
diagnostic for scientific comparison. The complete conditional covariance is
also computed explicitly; neither is an independently measured uncertainty.
The primary full-field log-conductivity inverse and output are unchanged in
physical scope, and are evaluated against actual author simulation truth.
